.e. it saw the future perimeter's geometry during training) and has NEVER seen a t0-window crop -- the ONLY geometry this live pipeline can ever produce at forecast time (the future perimeter is, by definition, unknown). So every live prediction from this model is out-of-distribution relative to its own training. The measured t0-window numbers above already reflect that (they are not a surprise), but this is 'best available', not 'production-ready' -- represent it that way. The operating_point (floor=0.0, mult=0.9) is the VAL-selected connected-causal decode point; it did NOT clear the 0.50 precision floor during selection (feasible=False, val P=0.270/R=0.259) -- it's the best-F1 fallback point, not a precision-guaranteed one.","issued_at_utc":"2026-08-14 12:40:14.410886+00:00","valid_from_utc":"2026-08-14 00:00:00","valid_to_utc":"2026-08-15 00:00:00","wfigs_date_current_utc":"2026-08-14 12:22:52+00:00","pixel_size_m":30,"veg_source":"refreshed_d4","physics_source":"eikonal_fbfm40","history_n_dates":1,"degraded_history":true,"containment_pct":85,"acres_wfigs":2623.1821664661975,"hour":16,"valid_at_utc":"2026-08-14 16:00:00"}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"MultiPolygon","coordinates":[[[[-100.30529,34.04912],[-100.30529,34.04886],[-100.30562,34.04886],[-100.30562,34.04859],[-100.30627,34.04859],[-100.30627,34.04886],[-100.30659,34.04886],[-100.30659,34.04912],[-100.30627,34.04912],[-100.30627,34.04966],[-100.30594,34.04966],[-100.30594,34.04912],[-100.30529,34.04912]]],[[[-100.30496,34.0564],[-100.30496,34.05667],[-100.30464,34.05667],[-100.30464,34.0564],[-100.30496,34.0564]]],[[[-100.30236,34.05694],[-100.30236,34.05721],[-100.30204,34.05721],[-100.30204,34.05694],[-100.30236,34.05694]]],[[[-100.30171,34.06368],[-100.30139,34.06368],[-100.30139,34.06341],[-100.30171,34.06341],[-100.30171,34.06368]]],[[[-100.3567,34.10599],[-100.3567,34.10626],[-100.35638,34.10626],[-100.35638,34.10653],[-100.3567,34.10653],[-100.3567,34.1068],[-100.3541,34.1068],[-100.3541